coder › Done. Everything is on `work/main` in two commits.

**What changed**

- **`src/csv.ts` (new)** — `parseCsv(text: string): string[][]`. Splits on `\n`, strips one trailing `\r` per line (so `\r\n` works), drops the final empty line from a trailing newline, and skips interior blank lines (they carry no fields). Per line: a field beginning with `"` is quoted, commas inside are literal, and `""` inside a quoted field is one `"`. An unclosed quote runs to end of line rather than erroring.
- **`src/cli.ts`** — added the `--json` branch: parses, returns `[]\n` for no rows, checks every data row against the header length, then emits `JSON.stringify` of objects keyed by header names + `\n`. All values are strings because they come straight out of `parseCsv`. Usage line now reads `usage: csvtool --upper | --count | --json`.
- **`src/csv.test.ts` (new)** — 9 parser tests: comma splitting, trailing-newline vs. empty fields/lines, `\r\n`, empty input, quoted commas, doubled quotes, quote closing against a comma, unclosed quote.
- **`src/cli.test.ts`** — 7 added tests: basic rows, empty input, header-only, string values with quotes/commas, `\r\n`, wrong field count, and the usage line mentioning `--json`.

